# Settings for the proxy modules deploy.local.sh deploys (watchdog, cms-augmentation).
#
# Copy to `.env` (QA, ENV=test) / `.env.uat` (ENV=uat) — both gitignored — and fill in.
# scripts/deploy.local.sh sources the file and bakes every @@NAME@@ token in the
# compiled .js with the value of NAME (see bake_js there).
#
# HOW A VALUE IS CHOSEN AT RUNTIME (the njs _setting helper), in order:
#   1. process.env[NAME] — an App Service app setting. Once Terraform sets it, it
#      wins over the baked value with no code change; the line here can then go.
#   2. the value baked in from this file at deploy time.
#   3. "" — there are NO hardcoded defaults. A missing value only breaks the routes
#      that need it (a 503 / a JSONP error); it can never stop nginx starting.
#
# The name IS the eventual app setting name, so this file doubles as the list to
# hand to Terraform. A live deploy stops if it is empty.

# The Watchdog (presence) API host — bare: no scheme, no path. Used by both the
# presence-jsonp adapter (as https://<host>/api) and the SignalR hub route.
# (The SignalR Service instance needs no setting: it is read from the Watchdog's
# own negotiate response.)
GLOBAL_COMPONENTS_WATCHDOG_HOST=app-cms-presence-api.azurewebsites.net

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not settings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CPS_PROXY_CONFIG_STORAGE_KEY — optional, deploy-time only: an account key for the
#   config storage account where the bastion's AAD identity lacks write access (UAT).
#   SECRET. Never baked into anything; only the az CLI sees it.
#
# nginx ${...} vars in the confs (${WEBSITE_DNS_SERVER}, ${WEBSITE_SCHEME},
# ${CMS_RATE_LIMIT_QUEUE}) are the PARENT project's app settings, rendered by the
# container's own envsubst at start. They are never baked.
#
# RETIRED 2026-11-10 — delete from your .env / .env.uat (the client secret most of all):
#   CPS_GLOBAL_COMPONENTS_CMS_AUTH_TENANT_ID, _CLIENT_ID, _CLIENT_SECRET,
#   _REDIRECT_URI, _PRESENCE_SCOPE   (the auth flow is Polaris's /init now)
#   CPS_GLOBAL_COMPONENTS_SIGNALR_HOST   (read from negotiate)
#   CPS_GLOBAL_COMPONENTS_WATCHDOG_HOST  (renamed GLOBAL_COMPONENTS_WATCHDOG_HOST;
#                                         deploy.local.sh still reads the old name
#                                         as a fallback, with a warning)
